.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_EVENT_ADD_CALLBACK 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_event_add_callback ,
.Nm ndi_event_remove_callback ,
.Nm ndi_event_run_callbacks ,
.Nm ndi_event_do_callback
.Nd register and deliver nexus event callbacks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_event_add_callback
.Fa "ndi_event_hdl_t handle"
.Fa "dev_info_t *child_dip"
.Fa "ddi_eventcookie_t cookie"
.Fa "ddi_event_cb_f event_callback"
.Fa "void *arg"
.Fa "uint_t flag"
.Fa "ddi_callback_id_t *cb_id"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_event_remove_callback
.Fa "ndi_event_hdl_t handle"
.Fa "ddi_callback_id_t id"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_event_run_callbacks
.Fa "ndi_event_hdl_t handle"
.Fa "dev_info_t *child_dip"
.Fa "ddi_eventcookie_t cookie"
.Fa "void *bus_impldata"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_event_do_callback
.Fa "ndi_event_hdl_t handle"
.Fa "dev_info_t *child_dip"
.Fa "ddi_eventcookie_t cookie"
.Fa "void *bus_impldata"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va handle
Event handle defining the cookie.
.It Va child_dip
Consumer node for registration, or target node for delivery.
.It Va cookie
Cookie bound to this handle.
.It Va event_callback
Function to invoke for the event.
.It Va arg
Opaque caller data passed to the callback.
.It Va flag
\fBNDI_SLEEP\fP or \fBNDI_NOSLEEP\fP for callback allocation.
.It Va cb_id
Output for the registration identifier.
.It Va id
Live registration identifier to remove.
.It Va bus_impldata
Event-specific data passed to each callback.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
\fBndi_event_add_callback()\fP registers \fBevent_callback\fP for \fBchild_dip\fP and
\fBcookie\fP, storing the registration identifier in \fB*cb_id\fP.
The cookie must be bound to \fBhandle\fP.
The framework stores \fBarg\fP without copying or owning the object it addresses.
Use \fBNDI_SLEEP\fP for sleeping allocation or \fBNDI_NOSLEEP\fP for allocation
that may fail rather than wait.
.Pp
\fBndi_event_remove_callback()\fP unregisters the live identifier \fBid\fP from the
same handle.
Use the identifier only once.
It must have been returned by successful registration on that handle;
arbitrary or already removed identifiers are not validated.
Remove registrations before their child detaches and before the event
definition or argument storage is destroyed.
.Pp
\fBndi_event_run_callbacks()\fP synchronously delivers the event according to
the definition's attributes.
For \fBNDI_EVENT_POST_TO_ALL\fP, every registered handler is called, in
unspecified order, and the supplied target does not restrict delivery.
For \fBNDI_EVENT_POST_TO_TGT\fP, only handlers registered for \fBchild_dip\fP are
called.
\fBndi_event_do_callback()\fP calls only the first matching registration for
\fBchild_dip\fP, regardless of the event's delivery attributes.
.Pp
Each callback is invoked as:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
void callback(dev_info_t *child, ddi_eventcookie_t cookie,
    void *arg, void *bus_impldata);
.Ed
The first three arguments come from the registration; the last is the
event-specific data supplied by the producer.
That data need only remain valid until synchronous delivery returns.
.Pp
Callbacks execute under the handle's callback-list lock.
They must not add or remove registrations, unbind events, free the handle,
or recursively deliver events on that handle.
They may use the local cookie conversion functions.
Removal synchronizes with callback delivery, allowing argument storage to
be released after removal returns, once other uses have also ended.
.Sh CONTEXT
Registration and removal may be called from user or kernel context.
Delivery and callbacks run in the producer's context and must obey the
priority restrictions specified by the event definition and handle locks.
Callbacks must not sleep while holding a spin lock or executing in interrupt
context.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Registration returns \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP, or \fBNDI_FAILURE\fP for an unknown
cookie or allocation failure.
Removal of a valid registration returns \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP.
Delivery returns \fBNDI_FAILURE\fP if the cookie is not bound to the handle,
and \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP otherwise, including when no callback matches.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_event_alloc_hdl 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_retrieve_cookie 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_definition 9S
